{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1157945-metamorphosis-and-attributes","id":1157945,"title":"Metamorphosis and attributes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-12T09:13:54-08:00","id":1157945,"title":"Metamorphosis and attributes","content":"The first dot of Metamorphosis says you can change physical things about someone (&quot;man into woman&quot; or a &quot;Nocker into a Boggan&quot;). Does this affect their attributes? Would a Nocker turned into a Boggan get the Boggan birthrights and lose the Nocker ones? What about physical things, like turning a weak person into a strong person? Or an ugly person into an attractive person?<br /> <br /> Does the power give mechanical benefits or is it purely &quot;for show&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16478-tristerfalm","name":"tristerfalm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T15:25:56-07:00","id":1242088,"title":"","content":"I know this is late, but having played a lot with metamorphosis recently here is my take.<br /> <br /> You can use Metamorphosis 1 to make someone stronger.<br /> <br /> You can use Metamorphosis 1 to make someone faster.<br /> <br /> You can use Metamorphosis 1 to make someone the opposite sex.<br /> <br /> What you cannot do is two of the above. One casting of metamorphosis 1 cannot change someone's sex and their strength. This may seem unrealistic, and it is. If you use metamorphosis 1 to change somebody's sex then it changes them into a member of the opposite sex who, however unlikely that may be, is identical to them in every other respect. Even hair length remains unchanged.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T15:41:28-07:00","id":1242100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daniel Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1157945-metamorphosis-and-attributes?p=1242088#post1242088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know this is late, but having played a lot with metamorphosis recently here is my take.<br /> <br /> You can use Metamorphosis 1 to make someone stronger.<br /> <br /> You can use Metamorphosis 1 to make someone faster.<br /> <br /> You can use Metamorphosis 1 to make someone the opposite sex.<br /> <br /> What you cannot do is two of the above. One casting of metamorphosis 1 cannot change someone's sex and their strength. This may seem unrealistic, and it is. If you use metamorphosis 1 to change somebody's sex then it changes them into a member of the opposite sex who, however unlikely that may be, is identical to them in every other respect. Even hair length remains unchanged.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think &quot;unrealistic&quot; makes sense as a critique. We're talking about magical powers here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T13:20:47-07:00","id":1245172,"title":"","content":"Don't get me wrong. I wasn't criticising it for being unrealistic.<br /> <br /> Realism is something Mages have to think about. Fairy magic is not realistic. If you turn Chuck Norris into a woman with Metamorphosis 1 he will become a woman who is like Chuck Norris in every way. If that is unrealistic, then people will shake their heads and mutter 'weird' as the mists take care of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T07:15:57-07:00","id":1248036,"title":"","content":"I think it's mostly cosmetic changes, but you could allow for each additional success to increase one Attribute by one (moving dots around doesn't 'cost' extra successes, but is included in the minimum number of successes required to perform the cantrip).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}